@@text
@@text Feature: [../creative_delight.md](../creative_delight.md) 10 (startup loader, helpers in Creative Common's jar, NCH namespace, CD
@@text script trees), tests CDT- in its section 19. Suite and how to load it: [tools/creative_delight_test/README.md](../../tools/creative_delight_test/README.md).
@@text Build `./gradlew :creativeCommon:build :creativeDelight:build -Pcd_test_suite --offline`; scratch `mods/`: the patcherMod jar and
@@text `creativedelight-1.0.0-cdtest.jar`, the three upstream member jars removed. Boot once for SQ-CDT-01 to -07, then the rows say what
@@text changes. Not run yet (owner: queue only).
@@text
@@table
## SQ-CDT-01
@group A
@commands Boot; `grep "jar-startup\|creativedelight\]\|cdtest\]" logs/kubejs/startup.log`
@pass `[jar-startup] creativeengineering: 3 of 3 files`, `[jar-startup] creativedelight: 2 of 3 files` (the `requires: cdtest_not_a_mod` file skipped), `startup script packs in order: creativeengineering, startup_scripts, ..., creativedelight`; `Neo Craft Helper finished` once; `[creativedelight] core finished, members: oceansdelight, oceanic_delight, ends_delight`; no startup script errors
@fails No `[jar-startup]` line: mixin not applied (`KubeJSStartupJarScriptsMixin`, require = 1 should have stopped boot); folder scripts erroring on `global.NCH` / `global.compost` undefined: Creative Common's pack not at the head
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-CDT-02
@group A
@commands `/cdtest startup`
@pass All PASS: helpers and dicts before the CD pack, ns at load `creativeengineering`, compost tiers > 0, requires honored
@fails Dict missing: the CD pack ran before the folder pack (order in `JarStartupScripts.addPacks`)
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-CDT-03
@group A
@commands Same boot: the pack's own startup and server scripts
@pass `logs/kubejs/startup.log` and `server.log` have no more errors than the last clean boot (compare counts); `/dumpcompost` still writes a table; recipes from `kubejs/server_scripts/cooking/` present (`/cdtest mirror` twins exist)
@fails A pack script used a top-level var of a moved helper (pack scopes are separate): give it a `global`
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-CDT-04
@group A
@commands `/cdtest ns`, `/cdtest requires`, `/cdtest tags`, `/cdtest config`
@pass All PASS; one expected `[NCH] withNamespace failed and was skipped: cdtest deliberate error` line in `server.log`
@fails Ids under `creativeengineering:`: `withNamespace` not used by `global.CD.recipes`; requires FAIL: header syntax in a data-pack script
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-CDT-05
@group A
@commands `/cdtest mirror`
@pass Every `twin of creativedelight:...` PASS (same type, result, ingredients as the pack's recipe); `twins made` PASS; NOTE lists about 30 helpers
@fails A twin differs: that helper builds something from the namespace besides the id; a twin missing: the call threw inside the CD block (grep `[NCH] ... failed`)
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-CDT-06
@group A
@commands `/reload`, then `/cdtest all`
@pass Same results as before the reload (server scripts from the jar reload); the deliberate `[NCH] withNamespace failed` line logged again (`server scripts ready` is a `ServerEvents.loaded` line: start only, not on `/reload`)
@fails Jar server scripts not reloaded: KubeJS keeps the first resource list
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-CDT-07
@group A
@commands Client on the scratch server (Round 2, or note it for CQ): hover a fishing net; F3+T
@pass Tooltip `[cdtest] tooltip from the Creative Delight client tree`; `logs/kubejs/client.log` has `[cdtest] client suite loaded, global.CD object` after F3+T too
@fails Client tree not read from the jar: check `assets/creativedelight/kubejs/` in the jar
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@client true
@draft needs a client (tooltip and client.log after F3+T) with the CD test jar: a CQ row on the capture driver
## SQ-CDT-08
@group A
@commands Stop; `config/creativedelight-common.toml` `[members] oceanic_delight = false`; boot; `/cdtest ns`, `/cdtest config`
@pass `member row follows CD.on()` PASS with `CD.on(oceanic_delight) false` and no `oceanic_member_row` recipe; Oceanic items still exist
@fails Switch ignored: `CDConfig.member` read before the config loaded at the wrong time
@jars creativecommon creativedelight
@draft needs its own boot with [members] oceanic_delight = false and the CD test jar (qrun cannot restart mid-batch): a separate boot batch
## SQ-CDT-09
