@@text
@@text ### Round 2: with a client window
@@text
@@text One JVM at a time (memory `one-game-instance-at-a-time`): this round is run with the scratch server stopped. Either a
@@text throwaway client on a single-player world (`tools/item_repro/launch_client.py GAME_DIR`, memory `client-launch-for-defaults`;
@@text fresh `config/`, so client defaults are the pack's) or the user's own game. A single-player world has the integrated
@@text server, so server probes (`/vtdtest`, `/fdtest`) also run there. Rows say what to look at; the full steps are in the
@@text named writeup test. Cheapest order: CQ-DUMP first (everything after the Vintage rows depends on it), then one creative
@@text superflat world for the visual groups, then a normal world for the world-feel groups.
@@text
@@text Planned (not built): [../client_capture.md](../client_capture.md) runs the capturable rows unattended and leaves one
@@text cropped PNG per test ID in `test_captures/`; once it exists these rows get a `Capture` column (spec / manual / partial).
@@text
